cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use stracers, please cite Laporte et al. (2013), who introduced the
  particle-tagging method, and Garavito-Camargo et al. (2019), who applied it to
  the stellar halo of the Milky Way. You can also cite the software itself.
type: software
title: "stracers: stellar tracers in N-body simulations"
abstract: >-
  stracers paints stellar haloes onto the dark matter particles of N-body
  simulations with the particle-tagging scheme of Laporte et al. (2013), and
  makes mock tracer populations, kinematics and catalogues from them.
authors:
  - family-names: Garavito-Camargo
    given-names: Nicolas
  - family-names: Laporte
    given-names: Chervin F. P.
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
